      "source_url": "https://thaqalayn.net/hadith/34/2/7/1",
      "text": [
        " : \"مَنِ اِشْتَرَى دَابَّةً فَلْيَقُمْ مِنْ جَانِبِهَا اَلْأَيْسَرِ وَ يَأْخُذُ نَاصِيَتَهَا بِيَدِهِ اَلْيُمْنَى وَ يَقْرَأُ عَلَى رَأْسِهَا فَاتِحَةَ اَلْكِتَابِ وَ \"قُلْ هُوَ اَللّٰهُ أَحَدٌ\" وَ اَلْمُعَوِّذَتَيْنِ وَ آخِرَ اَلْحَشْرِ وَ آخِرَ بَنِي إِسْرَائِيلَ \"قُلِ اُدْعُوا اَللّٰهَ أَوِ اُدْعُوا اَلرَّحْمٰنَ\" وَ آيَةَ اَلْكُرْسِيِّ فَإِنَّ ذَلِكَ أَمَانُ تِلْكَ اَلدَّابَّةِ مِنَ اَلْآفَاتِ\"."
      ],
      "translations": {
        "en.bab-ul-qaim-publications": [
          "Hadith.3759 - Umar ibn Ibrahim narrated from Abu Al-Hasan (as) who said:\n\"Whoever buys an animal should stand on its left side, hold its forelock with his right hand, and recite over its head:\nSurah Al-Fatiha: the Opening of the Book,\nSurah Al-Ikhlas (Qul Huwa Allahu Ahad),\nSurah Al-Falaq and Surah Al-Nas (the two Mu'awwidhatayn) - two chapters of seeking refuge\nThe last verses of Surah Al-Hashr,\nThe last verse of Surah Bani Isra'il (Al-Isra'): 'Say, call upon Allah (swt) or call upon the Most Merciful',\nAyat Al-Kursi\nVerily, this will serve as protection for the animal from afflictions.\""
        ]
      }
    },
